On 25 June the Conservative Party withdrew support for their candidate,<ref name="indy suspension"/> but it was quickly confirmed on behalf of the returning officer that his name and party designation had to remain on the ballot paper.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Luxon |first1=Debbie |title=Powys confirms Craig Williams will continue to stand for MP |url=https://www.cambrian-news.co.uk/news/powys-confirms-craig-williams-will-continue-to-stand-for-mp-699776 |access-date=30 June 2024 |work=Cambrian News |date=25 June 2024 |language=en}}</ref> On 20 June a [[YouGov]] poll had predicted Montgomeryshire and Glyndŵr would be the only seat in Wales to be won by the Conservatives, by a narrow margin.<ref>{{cite news |title=Just one Tory seat in Wales predicted after general election |url=https://www.westerntelegraph.co.uk/news/24400302.just-one-tory-seat-wales-predicted-general-election/ |access-date=1 July 2024 |work=Western Telegraph |date=20 June 2024 |language=en}}</ref>

