{{Short description|United Kingdom parliamentary constituency (2024–)}} {{Infobox UK constituency main |name = Mid and South Pembrokeshire |parliament = uk |image = {{maplink|frame=yes|frame-align=center|plain=yes|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Mid and South Pembrokeshire (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame-height=200|frame-width=250|zoom=SWITCH:8,6|switch=location of constituency, location within Wales|frame-latitude=SWITCH:51.76,52.3|frame-longitude=SWITCH:-5.10,-3.7 }} |caption = Interactive map of the constituency. |image2 = [[File:MidSouthPembrokeshire2024Constituency.svg|120px|alt=Map of constituency]] |caption2 = Location of the constituency within Wales |year = |abolished = |type = |elects_howmany = One |previous = |next = |population = |electorate = |mp = [[Henry Tufnell (Welsh politician)|Henry Tufnell]] |party = |region = Wales |county = |towns = |national = }} '''Mid and South Pembrokeshire''' ({{lang-cy|Canol a De Sir Benfro}}) is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]], first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election]]. It was created following the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]].
== Contents == The constituency comprises the following areas in [[Pembrokeshire]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=2023 Parliamentary Review - Revised Proposals {{!}} Boundary Commission for Wales |url=https://bcomm-wales.gov.uk/reviews/10-22/2023-parliamentary-review-revised-proposals |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=[[Boundary Commission for Wales]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Pembrokeshire Mid and South |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Pembrokeshire%20Mid%20and%20South |access-date=2023-07-30 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* Part of the former [[Carmarthen West and South Pembrokeshire (UK Parliament constituency)|Carmarthen West and South Pembrokeshire]] ** The wards of [[Amroth (electoral ward)|Amroth]] and Saundersfoot North, Carew and Jeffreyston, East Williamston, Hundleton, [[Kilgetty and Begelly]], Lampeter Velfrey, Lamphey, Manorbier and Penally, [[Martletwy (electoral ward)|Martletwy]], [[Narberth (electoral ward)|Narberth]], [[Narberth Rural]], Pembroke Dock Bufferland, Pembroke Dock Bush, Pembroke Dock Central, [[Pembroke Dock Market]], Pembroke Dock Pennar, [[Pembroke Monkton and St Mary South]], [[Pembroke St Mary North]], [[Pembroke St Michael]], Saundersfoot South, St Florence and St Mary Out Liberty, Tenby North, and Tenby South (34,332 electors in total)<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Pembrokeshire Mid and South |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Pembrokeshire+Mid+and+South |access-date=2024-05-30 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref> * Part of the former [[Preseli Pembrokeshire (UK Parliament constituency)|Preseli Pembrokeshire]] ** The wards of Burton, Camrose, Haverfordwest Castle, Haverfordwest Garth, Haverfordwest Portfield, Haverfordwest Prendergast, Haverfordwest Priory, Johnston, Letterston, Llangwm, Martletwy (the remaining 345 electors), Merlin's Bridge, Milford Central, Milford East, Milford Hakin, Milford Hubberston, Milford North, Milford West, Neyland East, Neyland West, Rudbaxton and Spittal, Solva, St David's, St Ishmael's, The Havens, and Wiston (42,446 electors in total)<ref name=":0" />
