==History==
Llanelli has traditionally been an ultra-safe [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] seat, with a Labour MP representing the constituency since 1922. It was represented by one-time deputy leader of the [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]], Jim Griffiths, from 1936 until his retirement in 1970. In recent years however Labour's majority had been somewhat eroded by [[Plaid Cymru]], who as of 2021 have won the [[Llanelli (Senedd constituency)|equivalent seat]] in the [[Senedd]] in two of the six Senedd elections to date. At the 2015 general election, however, the Labour majority increased once again.

