On 31 May Labour announced the selection of [[Torsten Bell]], chief executive of the [[Resolution Foundation]], as their candidate in the constituency. They were accused of "parachuting" their favoured candidate, against the wishes of local party members.<ref name="BBC parachute">{{cite news|first=Catrin Haf |last=Jones |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw993v797ggo |title=Labour criticised for 'parachuting' in candidate |work=BBC News |date=31 May 2024 |access-date=30 June 2024 }}</ref> Bell had no connection to Swansea or Wales. The previous MP, Geraint Davies, had been barred from standing because he was subject to an investigation.<ref name="BBC parachute" />
